\section{AI-assisted development log}
\label{app:ai}

\paragraph{Tools and models.} The code for this assignment was written with the help of an
AI coding agent (OpenCode) powered by the model \texttt{opencode/big-pickle} (``Big
Pickle''). The agent produced draft implementations, refactored scripts and suggested
debugging fixes. The audited foundation models (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct,
Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3, Phi-3.5-mini-instruct, Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct) were run locally
with Hugging Face \texttt{transformers}; no prompt text, response or dataset was sent to a
third-party inference API. Every generated file was read, executed on the A100 host, and
its outputs inspected; the numbers in this report come from those executions, not from the
agent's text.

\paragraph{Prompts used.} The following are the task prompts given to the coding agent,
abridged only where the same instruction was repeated for a later question.

\begin{enumerate}[label=\textbf{P\arabic*.},leftmargin=2.2em]
\item ``Design 20 original bias-audit prompts with two prompts each across at least ten
dimensions, including Indian/Global South contexts, caste/religion and religious
accommodation. Each item must be a counterfactual pair that changes exactly one attribute,
state a directional hypothesis, and request a concrete, scoreable output. Write a Python
generation script for Hugging Face chat models with temperature 0.7, top-p 0.9, three
seeds, resume support, and JSONL metadata.''
\item ``Write a deterministic annotation script: refusal, sentiment with a fixed
off-the-shelf classifier, item-specific favourability parsers, specificity, and curated
lexicons for stereotype, agency, communion, accommodation, respect, condescension,
discouragement, deficit, othering and risk language. Aggregate over seeds and store every
raw indicator.''
\item ``Write the statistical analysis: seed-matched paired deltas, pooled-SD composite
disparity, cluster bootstrap over items, Wilcoxon with Holm correction, Friedman and
pairwise tests across models, directional-hypothesis support, and publication-quality
figures.''
\item ``Implement two mitigations on the eight highest-disparity items: a fairness system
prompt and a counterfactual self-audit rewrite. Keep decoding settings and seeds identical
to the baseline so the comparison is paired.''
\item ``Implement FedAvg from scratch for five clients on a balanced 12,000/2,000
Fashion-MNIST subset with a small CNN. Compare IID, Dirichlet(0.5), Dirichlet(0.1) and a
two-class-per-client label skew against centralized training with the same architecture,
optimizer and number of passes. Report per-client accuracy and communication volume.''
\item ``Implement DP-SGD manually with \texttt{torch.func.vmap} per-example gradients,
clipping to $C$, Gaussian noise $\sigma C$ on the batch sum, and no BatchNorm. Run
$C\in\{1,5\}$, $\sigma\in\{0.4,0.8,1.2\}$, 15 epochs, and compute $\eps$ with the RDP and
PRV accountants at $\delta=10^{-5}$. Add ablations for 5/30 epochs and 6,000 examples.''
\item ``Implement membership inference with loss, confidence and entropy threshold
attacks plus a four-shadow-model logistic attack. Report ROC-AUC, TPR at 1\% and 10\% FPR
and advantage, and add an intentionally overfit non-private baseline so the attack has a
signal to detect.''
\item Debugging prompts, \eg: ``The Q3 aggregation crashes with \texttt{KeyError:
'config'}; fix it and save results incrementally after each configuration.'' ``The
mitigation analysis fails because \texttt{seed\_deltas} merges on
(model, item, seed) while two interventions produce duplicate rows; include the
intervention in the index.'' ``The baseline membership AUC is only 0.53; add a
deliberately overfit baseline to show the DP effect.''
\end{enumerate}

\paragraph{Verification.} All scripts were executed end-to-end on the A100 host. Results
were regenerated after every bug fix; the final artefacts are those referenced in
Table~\ref{tab:files}. No cell in this report was manually typed from memory: tables are
generated by \texttt{report/make\_tables.py} from the CSV/JSON files.

